  {
    "sha": "d0df089d8cc942dcd95252307ea75ac95808ed91",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKGQwZGYwODlkOGNjOTQyZGNkOTUyNTIzMDdlYTc1YWM5NTgwOGVkOTE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T02:00:12Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T02:00:12Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(tools): check insert and seat specs and normalize connections in a component\n\nToolComponent::new now runs InsertSpec::check and InsertSeatSpec::check\non the specs it is given, and names the component, the seat port and\nthe position in each refusal. check_insert_fit runs the same checks as\na guard. InsertSpec::check also confirms that the value is the parse of\nits own text. ConnectionCode::canonical gives the value that the code's\ntext parses to; the component stores it, and takes compares canonical\nforms, so a non-canonical typed code fits its canonical twin.\n\nRefs #3642\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
